{"kind":"report","text":"Confirm the proposed two-participant model, with the refinements below, as an explicit G2p-b initial support clarification of eae69004 paragraph 7. This is a pre-Source recommendation for planner adoption, not Source approval, an authority expansion or a public/session path switch. Current inspected baseline is landed G2p-a Main 3f1c9b2fae26b46d62d66dc53f6366fff7f18b93. Checked capture/current budget charges, native destination/rules/directory callbacks, repositorySessionBirth/recordedMembership and legacy session preparation.\n\n1. Permit at most two distinct preparation participants: the local reading scope, plus at most one exact actual birth directory when the existing unresolved-reference policy needs it. Each gets one inherited never-reset G2p-a PreparationBudget at its existing hard maxima. No second local budget, borrowing, top-up, recapture reset, additional peer, recursive discovery or automatic retry. A fully local path uses only its local allowance. A failure in either required participant stops the composite operation; unused allowance elsewhere cannot repair it. Keep the caller's original budget and frame through final revalidation. Treat a new attempt as a distinct explicitly admitted operation, not a hidden continuation/reset of this one.\n\n2. Aggregate preparation maxima are \u003c=32 calls, 32 metadata candidates, 512 KiB cumulative item/fold bodies, 128 KiB metadata reservations, 2 MiB reserved exact genesis, and 512 KiB admitted declared content. Calls means the existing conservative ledger: charged SQL/read operations AND charged native support/policy/cached-scope work, not a relabeling that silently drops those costs. Each participant is still capped at 16/16/256KiB/64KiB/1MiB/256KiB respectively, with the existing 4KiB scope-row, 2KiB key/cache identity and policy limits. Account all state lookahead, failed/read attempts, repeated work, support and final checks; actual lower usage does not entitle a participant to another reservation. Separately bound the fixed session-MAC/form/codec and single-RPC work. These totals describe this preparation model; they are not all Durable Object construction/background SQL, total copies, peak heap, physical I/O, global concurrent frames or a deployment resource bound. Ordinary independently owned bounded lifecycle maintenance retains the G2s/G2r qualifications; prove activation does not introduce legacy read/driver work through the new path.\n\n3. Native composition justifies separate genesis allowances. G2p-a platform capture currently conservatively costs six calls (scope, policy, three ProofBytes SQL and pin support); current() adds three (scope, policy, support). A destination branch page over empty/ready costs three calls and four metadata candidates; a zero-incarnation proof adds one call. repositorySessionBirth also asks for the current scope and repeats the held branch through recordedMembership. With existing uncached preparationView that one birth computation plus capture/current already costs seventeen calls, before repeated legacy prepare/resolve calls or a directory. The builder's fifteen-call local plan therefore relies on operation-local exact page reuse; it is not established by today's storage child alone. The native receiver independently needs its own genesis/pin, exact open-repository/cardinality/membership and current checks. A single aggregate one-genesis reservation cannot represent those two necessary local histories.\n\n4. Allow bounded operation-local reuse/factoring of the same pure native policy on a coherent frame, rather than executing the entire legacy prepare/resolve wrapper repeatedly. Cache keys bind full snapshot identity and exact validated page/ref arguments; retain only bounded successful immutable data/copies, and charge cache accesses conservatively. No standing membership/role/claim cache, cross-head item cache, truncated completeness or swallowed unavailable result. Unchanged final full-head/incarnation/genesis/status/time verification can justify reuse of that operation's native birth descriptor; a changed snapshot stops it. Preserve native exact catalog/cohort rules and rules/destination target asymmetry. Source must trace the actual complete caller and receiver operation, including cache hits and final checks, and demonstrate that each \u003c=16 allowance really fits supported native cases. Do not claim the proposed fifteen/twelve counts, all cohorts or all legal rooms as measured readiness from this decision.\n\n5. Admit one request \u003c=8192 actual UTF-8 bytes and one reply \u003c=2048 actual UTF-8 bytes, including version/identity/cohort/framing. Preflight finite shape/count/string limits before serialization/decode allocations, verify actual bytes and strict exact schema, and clamp in both native sender and receiver. Receiver does not trust caller-supplied numeric caps to increase its own allowance. Reply remains only the bounded reference witness authorized under existing session policy, never a summary/inventory/body. Caller chooses the peer solely from its validated native applied birth, not the token or reply. Receiver independently authenticates bounded MAC/form/deployment, clock/window, its own confirmed membership and the required summary claim before disclosing a witness. Unsupported capability or oversized/malformed/unbound reply fails unavailable with no old source/summary fallback. No receiver peer call is allowed.\n\n6. Start one absolute caller 10-second completion deadline before initial request validation/preparation. It covers local work, send/queue/receiver wait, final local metadata/support and the last fresh authority check. An individual peer helper must never start a new caller allowance. Native receiver also clamps its own finite work and checks a finite local remaining-time allowance; do not assume clocks share a monotonic epoch or claim caller cancellation physically stops receiver work. If a remaining duration is transmitted it is a subordinate cap, never authority or an extension of the caller deadline. Timeout ends caller completion as unknown/forbidden according to existing disclosure policy, with no late accepted witness/cache/authority. Preserve one bounded per-live-object admission/singleflight ownership until the outstanding task settles; do not release it merely because a caller timed out or a token expired. No recursion, automatic retry, fallback, unbounded queued waiter pool or physical cancellation/drain/cross-isolate/global cleanup claim. Check time after final metadata and before evidence/cache, and authenticate after all potentially blocking preparation as established by the G2r fixes.\n\n7. All eae69004 authority conditions remain: partial membership IDs cannot grant reads; unresolved fallback needs existing summary compatibility in addition to the requested live/final/mixed claims; a new query claim grants nothing by itself. Session claims keep their existing expiry/revocation semantics. Match current full scope/incarnation, exact catalog pin, judged birth directory, local membership ID/incarnation and the authorized returned full ref after awaits/cache hits. No new room-chain authority, current-role reinterpretation or public progress/head/size reason for an unproved caller. Receiver authorization is independent of caller filtering. Public query/legacy admission stay disabled in this support child.\n\n8. G2p-b remains unapproved until an exact Source review proves composed local-only and unresolved rules/destination paths with genuinely judged native cohorts, restricted live/final/mixed/summary-fallback claims, cross-repository/incarnation/cohort/target/cardinality refusals, exact counters/pre-body admission, final drift and expiry, never-settling/late peer behavior, owned pending capacity and no legacy/driver fallback. Preserve synthetic/layout/outside/clock/host qualifications. Per-function receiver tests and the G2p-a callback parity fixture are useful but do not prove this whole composition. No new test execution, gate, provider collection or deployment was requested by this decision. Planner can adopt these finite support limits while keeping G2p-b, public query and full G2/e029 completion open.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:15139985811def208d3de339b8c4e1a0224c7ea1","scope":"G2p-b two-participant aggregate preparation budget decision"}}